  <data name="Str_ConnFail.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Connection failures</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_PairFail.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pairing failed</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_NoDevAccess.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cannot access the device.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_NoDevAccessWhy.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This usually means:
1. The device is not paired with this PC yet - press "Pair" first;
2. The device exposes no GATT services (phones are generally not BLE peripherals);
3. Another program is using the device.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_UseKeyboardPage.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>To use this PC as a Bluetooth keyboard for a phone, use the "Virtual Keyboard" page instead: turn on advertising there, then pair from the phone.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_PairDenied.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The system denied access (AccessDenied). Common causes:
1. The device is not in discoverable/pairable mode;
2. It is already paired with another host - unpair it there first;
3. Windows Bluetooth permission is off: Settings &gt; Privacy &gt; Bluetooth.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_HidRadioOff.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>*** Detected: system Bluetooth is currently OFF ***</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_HidRadioOffFix.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Turn Bluetooth on first (Settings &gt; Bluetooth &amp; devices, or the taskbar quick settings), then flip the advertising switch above.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_HidRadioOnStillFails.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bluetooth is on but the advertising resource is still unavailable. Try in order:</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_HidSteps.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Close Phone Link / other apps that use Bluetooth;
2. Turn Bluetooth off, wait 5 s, turn it back on;
3. Device Manager &gt; Bluetooth &gt; Intel Wireless Bluetooth &gt; Disable then Enable;
4. Update the Intel Bluetooth driver;
5. Restart the PC and reopen this app.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_HidNeedPeripheral.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Note: this feature needs a Bluetooth adapter that supports the peripheral role.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_AdapterErr.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error getting access to the Bluetooth adapter. Is Bluetooth enabled?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_PairReq.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Please enter the PIN shown on the device.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_CannotPair.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This device cannot be paired right now. Make sure Bluetooth is on, it is discoverable, and not in use by another host.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_LangLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Language</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Str_LangRestart.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The app restarts automatically after switching language.</value>
  </data>
</root>
